# The raw-XML cache (~8.5 GB projected) and ledgers stay on pc1 — never committed.
# NOTE: `data/*` not `data/` — git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT dir is
# excluded, so an excluded `data/` would silently defeat the exception below.
# (Verified with `git check-ignore -v`; the naive `data/` + `!…` form FAILED.)
data/*

# EXCEPTION — the vision evidence ledger. The rule above exists because a script
# REGENERATES everything under data/. Nothing regenerates this: a vision call is
# non-reproducible (re-running the model returns a DIFFERENT answer), so the
# ledger is EVIDENCE, not derived data. On 2026-07-16 "has vision ever run?"
# needed a forensic audit precisely because the calls were never stored. 344 KB
# of text; the raw responses in it are irreplaceable and cost real money.
# The BLOBS stay ignored: ~4.6 MB/36 figures (~2 GB at corpus scale) and they are
# re-fetchable from the PMC CDN — and content-hashed, so drift is detectable.
!data/visionstore/
data/visionstore/*
!data/visionstore/calls.jsonl
# Same reasoning, per-shard. The exception is BY NAME because `data/visionstore/*`
# excludes the dir's contents wholesale; a shard added without its own `!` line is
# silently untracked, which is how irreplaceable evidence goes missing quietly.
# Shard writers append here to avoid interleaving with the owner's calls.jsonl;
# the owner merges. Blobs stay ignored (re-fetchable + content-hashed).
!data/visionstore/calls.shard-A.jsonl

__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc
# Local resume state: holds local paths + run state, not portable across nodes.
PROGRESS.md
